From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: retroforge <retroforge@invalid>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 08:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(LibraryMenu): a card is rebuilt when its library item is
 replaced

The library tabs kept a card per name. A library that drops a game and
adds it again leaves LibraryManager with a new LibraryItem of the same
name, and the Installed and All Games tabs kept their card on the old one,
which has no launch item: its art lookup found no game, so it showed the
placeholder, and Play had nothing to launch (HW, MANGMI Air X, 2026-10-24:
Hades, whose Steam desktop shortcut the RetroForge plugin drops in favour
of its Steam library's entry). The card listens for removed_from_library
only once it is built, and the removal came first.

As the home screen does since 0023, a card is now reused only while it
shows the very item; otherwise the old one is freed and a new one built.

---
 core/ui/card_ui/library/library_menu.gd | 15 +++++++++++----
 1 file changed

--- a/core/ui/card_ui/library/library_menu.gd
+++ b/core/ui/card_ui/library/library_menu.gd
@@ -185,11 +185,18 @@
 		if is_hidden:
 			continue
 		
-		# If the card node already exists, move it to the correct place
+		# If the card node already exists, move it to the correct place. Reuse one only while it
+		# shows this very item: a library that drops a game and adds it again makes a new
+		# LibraryItem of the same name, and a card left on the old one has no launch item (no art;
+		# Play does nothing). Its removed_from_library can come while the card is being built.
 		if tab_num in _library and item.name in _library[tab_num]:
-			var card := _library[tab_num][item.name] as GameCard
-			grid.move_child(card, i)
-			continue
+			var old = _library[tab_num][item.name]  # untyped: a freed card may still be listed
+			if is_instance_valid(old) and (old as GameCard).library_item == item:
+				grid.move_child(old, i)
+				continue
+			_library[tab_num].erase(item.name)
+			if is_instance_valid(old):
+				old.queue_free()
 		
 		# Build a card for each library item
 		var card := await _build_card(item)
